{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>El bringing them out of Egypt.</b> It says <b>bringing them out</b> (motzi'am) and not 'brought them out' (hotzi'am), even though our Sages of blessed memory said (Berakhot 38a) that 'motzi' conveys the present, and they proved it from here; nevertheless, the language of the past would be more clearly conveyed if it had said 'hotzi'am.' And it appears according to their saying, of blessed memory (Pesachim 116b), that in every generation a person is obligated to see himself as though he himself went out of Egypt — therefore the masters of the inner Torah said that every Passover night the forces of holiness are refined from the klippah and added to the people of Israel, and this is the very aspect of the Exodus from Egypt itself. And this is what it says, <b>El bringing them out</b> — for it is not the first exodus alone, but in every single year He brings them out, as mentioned. And He gave a reason: <b>like the loftiness of a re'em for him</b> — meaning, that HaShem increases and strengthens them to elevate them, and there is no end to the loftiness that HaShem intends for them, until the boundary that no admixture of evil at all remains in the holiness. And this is what it says, <b>for there is no divination in Jacob</b> — an allusion to the aspect of nichush [divination], and also to the aspect of that which is called nachash [serpent], which is the head of the klippah, Samekh-Mem the wicked, who is called nachash — that it will be uprooted and nothing of it will remain in Jacob, as it says (Zechariah 13:2): ״וְאֶת רוּחַ הַטֻּמְאָה אַעֲבִיר מִן הָאָרֶץ״. ״וְלֹא קֶסֶם״ — this is an aspect of impurity below it, and then Israel will be in the category of perfection of degree and their excellence will surpass that of the angels. And this is what he concludes saying, <b>According to this time it shall be said of Jacob</b> etc., and our Sages of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah 20:20) that the angels will ask Israel: ״מַה פָּעַל אֵל״."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The abbreviation ס״מ is resolved as Samekh-Mem, the standard circumlocution for the adversary (Sama'el-Mavet). The verse citation Zechariah 13:2 is normalized from the Hebrew form זכריה י״ג:ב׳."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:13:26.919199988Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}